From 6e4c8f402735dc6eb8ce35175e92d80a257da308 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 03:42:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/12] feat(proton): install DroidDeck-Proton rewritten for
 ARMv8.0 CPUs

Every arm64 Proton build stops with SIGILL on Cortex-A53/A73 (no LSE
atomics). On such a CPU the session now installs DroidDeck-Proton
11-12.8 with a bundled patch (tools/armv80/rewrite_tree.py output, 688
files, 53,158 sites): the pinned release is verified by sha256, every
patched file is checked before and after, and the result is a separate
tool, "DroidDeck-Proton 11-12.8 (ARMv8.0)", marked .droiddeck-armv80.

The x86-64 Steam client defaults to that tool and only marked arm64
Protons are bridged; droiddeck-proton-x64 stays the fallback. The app
no longer auto-installs the stock arm64 Protons on these CPUs.

Verified on an emulated Cortex-A53 (QEMU system, kernel 6.8): wine
starts, x86 (WoW64) and x86-64 (ARM64EC) Windows test programs run
through FEX with correct atomics, threads and FP, with and without
fsync.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
